Description: Tools to fit, compare, and plot individual growth models
    (von Bertalanffy, Gompertz, Gompertz-Laird, logistic, Richards, the four
    classic Schnute (1981) parametrisation cases, Schnute-Richards, a
    seasonal von Bertalanffy model, alternative von Bertalanffy
    reparametrisations, a practical biphasic model, the non-asymptotic
    Persistence and Tanaka models, four classical single-predictor
    baseline curves (linear, power, exponential, and logarithmic), and
    seven further named curves from the growth-model literature
    (hyperbolic, Ricker, Beverton-Holt, Gamma, Weibull, extended power,
    and Johnson) under a
    multi-model approach. Includes
    fitting by nonlinear least squares, maximum likelihood, or Bayesian
    inference (self-contained adaptive Metropolis-Hastings MCMC, no external
    engine required); confidence/credible intervals via likelihood profiles
    (with profile plots), joint (bivariate) likelihood-profile confidence
    regions for correlated parameter pairs, bootstrap, or posterior
    samples; model comparison
    via information criteria (AIC, AICc, BIC) with Akaike weights or
    Bayesian criteria (WAIC, DIC); model-averaged predictions; growth-curve
    comparison between groups via group-covariate model fitting and the
    Kimura (1980)/Cerrato (1990) likelihood-ratio test; results tables;
    elegant 'ggplot2' plots; runtime registration of user-defined
    growth models (add_growth_model()) so the built-in catalogue can be
    extended with any custom curve, with an automatic multi-start search
    for starting values so a starting-value heuristic is not required; and
    growth rate (dL/dt) calculation and plotting (growth_rate(),
    plot_growth_rate()), absolute and/or relative, computed numerically so
    it works for any model, built-in or custom.
